  "title": "Ross Shows Mosquitoes Transmit Malaria",
  "summary": "While working in Secunderabad, India, the British physician Ronald Ross let mosquitoes feed on a malaria patient on 16 August 1897. Dissecting one on 20 August, he found the parasite in its stomach tissue, a key step in showing mosquitoes carry malaria. He received the 1902 Nobel Prize for this work.",
